  "$comment": "FEED-200: the horizontal swipe pager, HAND-AUTHORED and replayed by packages/exponential-ui/src/swipe.test.ts (the TS reference the web renderers use), apps/desktop/crates/eui-core/tests/swipe.rs (the core: gpui and the surface's Tabs pager) and the FFI through packages/exponential-ui-swift + packages/exponential-ui-compose tests. `Tabs.swipeable` pages its panels with these rules; FEED-201 reuses them for app screens. Offsets/velocities = SCREEN px (px/ms), positive = rightwards; `rtl` mirrors which neighbour a drag reveals. constants = the shared numbers. lock = swipeLock(dx, dy): `pending` inside the slop, `horizontal` when |dx| > |dy|, else `vertical`. step = swipeStep(offset, rtl): left reveals the next page (LTR). offset = swipeOffset(index, count, offset, width, rtl): the drawn offset, `resistance` of the travel past an end, clamped to one width. settle = swipeSettle(index, count, offset, velocity, width, rtl) → the page a release lands on: one step towards the drag on a fling (|velocity| >= `velocity`, same sign as the offset, offset >= `slop`) or past `distance` x width unless flung back; never past an end. progress = swipeProgress(offset, width) (0..1, what the header indicator interpolates by). indicator = swipeIndicator(from, to, progress) → {x, w}. blocks = swipeBlocks(component, direction, overflowX): a touch starting inside a node that scrolls, pans or drags sideways is that node's, never the pager's. Compare numbers within 1e-6.",
